   <p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">Accounts receivable for all segments represent invoicing for products with varying payment terms, but with <em style="font: inherit;">no</em> variable consideration or financing. The opening balance of accounts receivable for all segments as of <em style="font: inherit;"> January 1, </em><em style="font: inherit;">2024</em>, was $<ix:nonFraction id="c141962541" contextRef="i_2024-01-01" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:AccountsReceivableNet" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-5">8.6</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million, and the closing balances as of <em style="font: inherit;"> December 31, 2025 </em>and <em style="font: inherit;">2024</em>, were $<ix:nonFraction id="c141962543" contextRef="i_2025-12-31" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:AccountsReceivableNet" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-5">0.5</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million and $<ix:nonFraction id="c141962544" contextRef="i_2024-12-31" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:AccountsReceivableNet" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-5">1.8</ix:nonFraction> million, respectively.</p>
   <p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">&#160;&#160;&#160;</p>
